---
import Section from "../site/Section.astro"
import Split from "../site/Split.astro"
import Stage from "../site/Stage.astro"
import ObservationBlocks from "../product/ObservationBlocks.astro"
---

<Section>
  <Split rev>
    <div slot="start" data-in-view="rise">
      <Stage><ObservationBlocks /></Stage>
    </div>
    <div slot="end" class="copy">
      <h2 class="h2">Text, panels and snapshots on one page.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        A panel block is a copy of a dashboard panel with its own query, and it stays live on the page. A snapshot freezes the data of a
        live panel at one moment, so the page keeps showing what you saw.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        A panel or snapshot block names who added it, a person or Observe Agent. Someone who can only comment suggests a block instead,
        and a person who can edit keeps it or discards it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Split>
</Section>

<style>
  .copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .copy .lead {
    font-size: 17px;
  }
</style>
